196
00:22:46,116 --> 00:22:47,520
He deserves to die.

197
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:51,440
Once you kill someone, you'll never sleep soundly again.

198
00:22:52,595 --> 00:22:54,250
You have a father who loves you and is waiting for you.

199
00:22:54,755 --> 00:22:56,100
Go back and live your life with him.

200
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:01,240
Some people would give anything to have that chance, but they don't.

201
00:23:04,291 --> 00:23:06,150
He killed my mother and my brother.

202
00:23:06,334 --> 00:23:08,200
And he left my father disabled.

203
00:23:08,270 --> 00:23:10,360
If I can't kill him, I'm the one who'll never sleep soundly again.

204
00:23:12,731 --> 00:23:14,352
You were going to kill Dongyang with massage, weren't you?

205
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,601
Like when you kissed me and knocked me out?

206
00:23:20,856 --> 00:23:21,857
Don't be ridiculous.

207
00:23:22,707 --> 00:23:24,400
Have you ever kissed a woman, Mr. Bodyguard?

208
00:23:34,046 --> 00:23:35,047
You didn't pass out.

209
00:23:41,528 --> 00:23:43,130
You can't beat us.

210
00:23:53,971 --> 00:23:56,000
Okay, I'll be right there.

211
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:04,280
Mr. Dongyang is safe.

212
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:57,200
What kind of security is this?

213
00:24:57,590 --> 00:24:58,960
How could you let this happen?

214
00:24:59,419 --> 00:25:00,840
That massage therapist, Hattha, snuck onto the boat.

215
00:25:01,072 --> 00:25:03,160
I called Phat, but we barely got there in time.

216
00:25:04,219 --> 00:25:05,978
Why would she want to hurt Mr. Dongyang?

217
00:25:06,918 --> 00:25:07,919
I don't know.

218
00:25:08,886 --> 00:25:11,211
When I went in, I saw Mr. Dongyang on top of her.

219
00:25:12,224 --> 00:25:13,225
Then he collapsed.

220
00:25:18,232 --> 00:25:20,120
She tried to kill me.

221
00:25:21,700 --> 00:25:22,701
How?

222
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:24,501
How?

223
00:25:25,915 --> 00:25:27,760
That damn Hattha.

224
00:25:31,403 --> 00:25:33,920
She's the daughter of that massage therapist in Phuket.

225
00:25:35,016 --> 00:25:36,017
Phuket?

226
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:41,100
She's here to avenge her parents.

227
00:25:50,478 --> 00:25:51,479
Phat!

228
00:25:52,856 --> 00:25:55,347
Round up her and all her relatives.

229
00:25:57,902 --> 00:25:59,720
Bring them to me alive.

230
00:26:00,798 --> 00:26:01,799
Muk.

231
00:26:03,224 --> 00:26:04,240
Stay here and look after Mr. Dongyang.

232
00:26:05,406 --> 00:26:06,407
I'm going with Phat.

233
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:09,301
Yes, Master.

234
00:26:17,846 --> 00:26:18,847
Dad!

235
00:26:20,902 --> 00:26:21,903
Dad!

236
00:26:22,358 --> 00:26:24,440
Dad, please. Don't go back yet. Just a little longer.

237
00:26:24,459 --> 00:26:25,800
- I'm so close, Dad.
- Close to what?

238
00:26:27,254 --> 00:26:28,560
You mean successfully killing someone?

239
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:31,220
How many more people are you going to kill?

240
00:26:31,718 --> 00:26:33,880
Dongyang, Flatfoot,

241
00:26:34,646 --> 00:26:36,000
and his men too, right?

242
00:26:37,579 --> 00:26:38,720
If you kill them,

243
00:26:39,622 --> 00:26:41,195
you'll be no different from them.

244
00:26:44,027 --> 00:26:45,560
I'm all packed, Uncle. Shall we go?

245
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:47,241
Wan!

246
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,900
Do you want to heal people or kill  people?

247
00:26:50,747 --> 00:26:52,230
If you go any further down this path,

248
00:26:52,902 --> 00:26:54,720
there'll be no turning back, Hattha.

249
00:26:57,683 --> 00:27:00,027
Using the art of healing massage to kill people...

250
00:27:01,043 --> 00:27:02,846
the consequences will come back to haunt you.

251
00:27:03,971 --> 00:27:05,920
And you'll become the very kind of person you hate.

252
00:27:07,540 --> 00:27:08,880
We're going home. Now.

253
00:27:15,235 --> 00:27:16,526
It's because of this journal, isn't it?

254
00:27:17,683 --> 00:27:19,560
This is what made you so sure you could do it.

255
00:27:22,542 --> 00:27:23,543
- Dad!
- Go!

256
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:27,290
Please stay. Wan, come on.

257
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:29,440
- Hattha, go home.
- No, stay.

258
00:27:29,566 --> 00:27:30,760
Dad! Wan!

259
00:27:30,936 --> 00:27:31,937
Wan! Let me go!

260
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:33,960
Dad! Dad!

261
00:27:38,254 --> 00:27:39,255
Dad!

262
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:46,771
Hey, it's on fire.

263
00:27:50,952 --> 00:27:51,953
Hattha!

264
00:27:52,206 --> 00:27:53,207
Hattha!

265
00:28:05,230 --> 00:28:07,320
Her hands are blistered. That must hurt.

266
00:28:08,582 --> 00:28:10,383
Physical pain is nothing compared to a broken heart.

267
00:28:14,624 --> 00:28:15,785
What about the journal?

268
00:29:00,142 --> 00:29:01,320
Master Tim is on his way.

269
00:29:13,459 --> 00:29:14,920
Who's with Hattha?

270
00:29:16,302 --> 00:29:17,840
Her older brother, Wan,

271
00:29:18,784 --> 00:29:21,000
her father, and a caretaker.

272
00:29:22,886 --> 00:29:23,887
Her real father?

273
00:29:25,558 --> 00:29:26,559
I'm not sure.

274
00:29:28,250 --> 00:29:29,251
But he's disabled.

275
00:29:38,334 --> 00:29:40,526
Isn't he one of Dongyang's men?

276
00:29:40,686 --> 00:29:42,600
Then why did he warn us that they're coming to our house?

277
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,000
No time for questions. We need to go.

278
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:55,640
Wan, get inside. Hurry! They're here. Go!

279
00:30:12,379 --> 00:30:13,650
They might know what we're up to.

280
00:30:14,315 --> 00:30:15,316
Check around the house too.

281
00:30:15,515 --> 00:30:17,116
Hey, check the back.

282
00:30:20,516 --> 00:30:21,517
Go! Go!

283
00:30:29,526 --> 00:30:30,527
Wan, what do we do?

284
00:30:41,091 --> 00:30:42,240
Uncle, get on my back.

285
00:30:43,491 --> 00:30:44,492
Come on, Dad.

286
00:30:50,176 --> 00:30:51,979
It's okay. It's okay. Just go!

287
00:32:45,502 --> 00:32:46,503
They're not here.

288
00:32:47,347 --> 00:32:48,348
Damn it!

289
00:33:50,392 --> 00:33:52,574
Master!

290
00:33:53,315 --> 00:33:55,000
- You found them?
- Yeah.

291
00:34:01,571 --> 00:34:02,572
They escaped out the back.

292
00:34:13,616 --> 00:34:14,617
Hattha!

293
00:34:30,411 --> 00:34:32,840
Ram them. Keep your head down. Trust me.

294
00:34:51,054 --> 00:34:52,055
Shoot out their tires!

295
00:34:53,587 --> 00:34:54,588
Everybody, get down!

296
00:34:57,032 --> 00:34:58,480
Watch out! Move!

297
00:35:06,220 --> 00:35:07,440
What the hell are you doing?

298
00:35:08,021 --> 00:35:09,160
I told you to shoot the tires!

299
00:35:34,683 --> 00:35:36,100
Can you go home with me now?

300
00:35:37,584 --> 00:35:38,800
But we made it out alive.

301
00:35:38,891 --> 00:35:39,892
Hattha.

302
00:35:40,534 --> 00:35:42,400
All clear. We can go now.

303
00:35:43,526 --> 00:35:44,840
Drive straight back to Photharam.

304
00:35:45,165 --> 00:35:46,166
Yes, sir.

305
00:35:49,464 --> 00:35:50,465
Wait.

306
00:35:51,928 --> 00:35:53,600
Why did that bodyguard help you?

307
00:35:55,744 --> 00:35:56,880
You know him, don't you?

308
00:36:01,851 --> 00:36:03,300
Yeah…I guess.

309
00:36:31,358 --> 00:36:32,480
Hattha, you bitch.

310
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:36,000
She must've used the deadly massage technique.

311
00:36:37,726 --> 00:36:38,727
How did she know it?

312
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:41,100
How did she know?

313
00:36:45,678 --> 00:36:47,280
Uncle!

314
00:36:47,715 --> 00:36:48,798
Uncle!

315
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:50,720
- Uncle!
- What is it?

316
00:36:51,272 --> 00:36:52,900
- Be careful.
- What is going on?

317
00:36:52,904 --> 00:36:54,800
I woke up and Hattha was gone.

318
00:36:54,905 --> 00:36:56,480
But she left a note.

319
00:36:56,880 --> 00:36:57,881
Let me see.

320
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:01,720
Once everything's taken care of, I'll come back as soon as I can.

321
00:37:02,174 --> 00:37:04,702
I promise I'll take good care of myself. —Hattha

322
00:37:07,798 --> 00:37:08,799
What's wrong, Korn?

323
00:37:10,872 --> 00:37:12,300
I knew this would happen.

324
00:37:27,328 --> 00:37:29,718
I'm not lying, Wan.

325
00:37:29,974 --> 00:37:32,219
Hattha really didn't come to see me.

326
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:33,640
She didn't call me either.

327
00:37:35,200 --> 00:37:36,760
Okay, okay.

328
00:37:36,990 --> 00:37:40,700
If Hattha calls me back or I hear anything from her,

329
00:37:41,006 --> 00:37:43,007
I'll let you know right away.

330
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,281
Okay.

331
00:37:46,768 --> 00:37:48,100
Thank you so much.

332
00:37:48,358 --> 00:37:49,700
But I won't be staying long.

333
00:37:50,159 --> 00:37:51,400
Please don't tell anyone I'm here yet.

334
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:53,320
So what's going on?

335
00:37:53,635 --> 00:37:55,520
You showed up out of nowhere in the middle of the night.

336
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:58,300
Is there something I should know?

337
00:37:59,902 --> 00:38:00,903
No.

338
00:38:02,835 --> 00:38:04,240
Since when did you get so good at lying?

339
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:08,840
Korn! Hi. How have you been?

340
00:38:09,165 --> 00:38:10,195
Not too well, actually.

341
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:12,840
- I had a fight with my daughter.
- Oh!

342
00:38:15,464 --> 00:38:17,400
- Wan.
- Yes?

343
00:38:18,259 --> 00:38:19,360
Get her back home.

344
00:38:21,334 --> 00:38:23,700
- Hattha, go home.
- Wan.

345
00:38:23,838 --> 00:38:25,500
- Let's go.
- Come on.

346
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:28,501
Korn!

347
00:38:28,520 --> 00:38:30,521
- What is going on?
- Go home!

348
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,040
Where are you going?

349
00:38:32,680 --> 00:38:34,360
Hattha, go home.

350
00:38:34,881 --> 00:38:35,882
Wan!

351
00:38:36,224 --> 00:38:37,225
Muk?

352
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:57,301
Korn.

353
00:38:59,011 --> 00:39:00,440
I thought you were fucking dead.

354
00:39:07,275 --> 00:39:11,000
Thirty-five years. You really thought you could hide from me forever?

355
00:39:12,134 --> 00:39:13,360
I trusted you.

356
00:39:13,584 --> 00:39:15,640
I had you help me find a deadly massage technique

357
00:39:15,776 --> 00:39:17,960
that could kill someone without them even realizing it.

358
00:39:25,627 --> 00:39:26,628
Is he dead?

359
00:39:26,768 --> 00:39:29,440
No, he's not dead. He's just unconscious.

360
00:39:30,022 --> 00:39:31,023
Hey, Tim.

361
00:39:31,768 --> 00:39:33,369
I think that's enough. I feel sorry for him.

362
00:39:33,944 --> 00:39:35,120
How can we stop now?

363
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:36,920
We still haven't succeeded.

364
00:39:37,752 --> 00:39:40,240
We still don't know which pressure point

365
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:41,600
can kill someone without them even realizing it.

366
00:39:42,910 --> 00:39:45,500
When he wakes up, you can try another spot.

367
00:39:46,424 --> 00:39:47,425
Damn it.

368
00:40:11,915 --> 00:40:12,916
The guiding point.

369
00:40:23,062 --> 00:40:24,080
The surrounding point.

370
00:40:29,195 --> 00:40:30,720
Then this must be...

371
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,170
the death point.

372
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:52,440
The final one.

373
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:54,920
The death point.

374
00:41:01,528 --> 00:41:04,374
I'm glad you're still alive.

375
00:41:06,208 --> 00:41:09,809
I heard about what happened to your family ten years ago.

376
00:41:11,494 --> 00:41:12,495
I'm sorry.

377
00:41:13,024 --> 00:41:15,414
Thank you. What about you?

378
00:41:17,419 --> 00:41:18,420
How have you been?

379
00:41:19,456 --> 00:41:20,457
Good.

380
00:41:22,613 --> 00:41:23,720
You never came to see me.

381
00:41:25,248 --> 00:41:26,249
Well...

382
00:41:27,616 --> 00:41:29,180
It's not easy for me to get around.

383
00:41:32,478 --> 00:41:33,479
She's your daughter?

384
00:41:34,910 --> 00:41:35,930
What a small world.

385
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:39,163
No wonder she's so good. Now I know where she gets it from.

386
00:41:40,435 --> 00:41:41,436
Tim

387
00:41:43,064 --> 00:41:46,707
If my daughter did anything to offend you,

388
00:41:47,427 --> 00:41:49,100
I apologize on her behalf.

389
00:41:49,875 --> 00:41:51,000
Please let her go.

390
00:41:51,995 --> 00:41:53,160
She's still young and doesn't know any better.

391
00:41:53,318 --> 00:41:54,440
Doesn't know any better?

392
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:56,880
Looking like that?

393
00:41:58,939 --> 00:41:59,940
She's old enough to have a husband.

394
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:04,840
But you need to teach her better.

395
00:42:06,502 --> 00:42:09,776
If you're going to strike a snake, make sure you kill it.

396
00:42:11,768 --> 00:42:13,805
Otherwise, it'll come back and bite you.

397
00:42:15,859 --> 00:42:17,040
Don't worry.

398
00:42:17,486 --> 00:42:20,568
I'll take my daughter back home to the countryside,

399
00:42:21,278 --> 00:42:22,654
and we'll never come back here again.

400
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:25,081
I'll be going now, Tim.

401
00:42:26,819 --> 00:42:27,840
Wan. Hattha.

402
00:42:29,582 --> 00:42:30,583
Hey!

403
00:42:31,814 --> 00:42:32,920
Hey! Hey!

404
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:36,920
I can help treat you so you can walk again.

405
00:42:47,859 --> 00:42:48,860
- Master?
- Master?

406
00:42:50,060 --> 00:42:51,061
Are you okay?

407
00:42:59,419 --> 00:43:00,420
Hattha.

408
00:43:02,078 --> 00:43:03,960
- You need to apologize to him.
- Dad.

409
00:43:04,734 --> 00:43:06,160
Apologize to him now.

410
00:43:16,782 --> 00:43:18,280
- Hattha.
- Hey!

411
00:43:48,224 --> 00:43:49,622
You went all the way there and found them.

412
00:43:49,638 --> 00:43:51,015
How could you just let them go?

413
00:43:51,366 --> 00:43:53,500
Are you going to wait until she tries to kill me again?

414
00:43:54,323 --> 00:43:56,163
I have something important to discuss with them.

415
00:43:56,744 --> 00:43:58,254
That's your business.

416
00:43:59,276 --> 00:44:02,080
Any of you who see her,

417
00:44:02,513 --> 00:44:03,614
take her out.

418
00:44:06,747 --> 00:44:12,360
If any of you find her, bring her to me first.

419
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:15,001
I'll deal with her myself.

420
00:44:26,120 --> 00:44:27,121
Don't worry.

421
00:44:29,571 --> 00:44:30,840
Your muscles are going to be tight.

422
00:45:34,659 --> 00:45:36,640
You followed me all the way here from the hospital.

423
00:45:36,755 --> 00:45:38,000
What are you still standing there thinking about?

424
00:45:40,155 --> 00:45:42,520
I'm here to collect the massage fee you still owe me.

425
00:45:48,542 --> 00:45:50,291
I want to stay here for a while.

426
00:45:52,803 --> 00:45:54,611
Until you manage to kill Dongyang?

427
00:45:56,350 --> 00:45:58,300
Aren't you afraid I'll turn you over to Dongyang?

428
00:45:58,351 --> 00:45:59,352
You wouldn't do that.

429
00:46:00,352 --> 00:46:02,360
Otherwise, you wouldn't have helped me so many times.

430
00:46:06,059 --> 00:46:07,560
I'm here to ask for your help.

431
00:46:08,830 --> 00:46:11,027
My dad wants to take me back to Photharam, but I don't want to go.

432
00:46:18,792 --> 00:46:19,793
Fine.

433
00:46:21,283 --> 00:46:22,718
But you have to give me a massage first.

434
00:46:23,242 --> 00:46:24,360
What's with you?

435
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:26,606
Someone's asking for treatment. Aren't you going to help?

436
00:46:27,155 --> 00:46:29,200
- Don't you want to heal people?
- It's not the time.

437
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,220
Do you choose when to make your move?

438
00:46:32,758 --> 00:46:33,920
What about the method?

439
00:46:34,854 --> 00:46:35,920
Do you choose that too?

440
00:46:38,219 --> 00:46:39,220
What?

441
00:46:39,734 --> 00:46:40,735
The massage.

442
00:46:41,686 --> 00:46:42,784
You want a deep massage, right?

443
00:46:45,595 --> 00:46:46,596
Fine.

444
00:46:59,544 --> 00:47:00,880
The Swallow Glides with the Wind.

445
00:47:11,187 --> 00:47:12,680
The Lion Bows and Snaps Its Neck.

446
00:47:24,323 --> 00:47:25,880
Massage can kill someone, can't it?

447
00:47:27,798 --> 00:47:28,799
What?

448
00:47:32,046 --> 00:47:33,718
There are vulnerable points on the human body.

449
00:47:34,774 --> 00:47:35,775
Press the right one, and you can kill someone.

450
00:47:36,619 --> 00:47:38,440
What have you been reading? Or have you been watching too many movies?

451
00:47:40,448 --> 00:47:41,960
The Sideways Stretch.

452
00:47:45,824 --> 00:47:48,520
If it were that easy, we wouldn't need massage therapists, would we?

453
00:47:48,806 --> 00:47:50,700
Every massage therapist knows the body's vulnerable points.

454
00:47:51,264 --> 00:47:52,720
They already know to avoid them.

455
00:47:53,030 --> 00:47:54,800
And it's not just massage therapists. Even patients know

456
00:47:55,104 --> 00:47:56,400
where the body's vulnerable points are.

457
00:47:56,912 --> 00:47:58,803
Even if a skilled massage therapist tried to press one,

458
00:47:59,320 --> 00:48:01,120
the moment it hurt, the person would pull away.

459
00:48:02,291 --> 00:48:03,800
So how could you possibly kill someone with massage?

460
00:48:05,592 --> 00:48:06,593
Think about it.

461
00:48:16,384 --> 00:48:17,792
The Cobra Sways Its Head.

462
00:48:20,536 --> 00:48:22,760
But I saw your hand on Mr. Dongyang's neck.

463
00:48:24,766 --> 00:48:26,640
Don't change the subject just to protect your boss.

464
00:48:27,278 --> 00:48:28,500
I'm the victim here.

465
00:48:31,816 --> 00:48:32,817
Push forward.

466
00:48:37,934 --> 00:48:39,340
The Tiger Circles the Cave.

467
00:49:03,526 --> 00:49:05,472
If you keep tensing up like this, I can't apply any pressure.

468
00:49:06,112 --> 00:49:07,300
No massage is going to fix it.

469
00:49:56,512 --> 00:49:57,560
Feel any better?

470
00:50:17,345 --> 00:50:18,440
You're stressed, aren't you?

471
00:50:20,054 --> 00:50:21,720
Sometimes you need to let things go.

472
00:50:22,305 --> 00:50:25,120
It'll help loosen up these tight muscles a little.

473
00:50:28,592 --> 00:50:30,450
Sometimes you have to let yourself make mistakes.

474
00:50:32,955 --> 00:50:34,480
It's exhausting trying to be good all the time.

475
00:50:54,024 --> 00:50:55,920
He killed my mother and my brother.

476
00:50:56,160 --> 00:50:57,961
And he left my father disabled.

477
00:50:58,046 --> 00:51:00,072
If I can't kill him, I'm the one who'll never sleep soundly again.

478
00:51:09,155 --> 00:51:10,942
Do you really want to be a murderer that badly?

479
00:51:12,174 --> 00:51:14,600
If I can kill Dongyang, I don't care what I become.

480
00:51:16,198 --> 00:51:18,840
Once you do it, you'll never be the same person again.

481
00:51:21,029 --> 00:51:22,579
Go home with your father.

482
00:51:26,600 --> 00:51:29,801
I refuse to be the same person, consumed by what he did to my family.

483
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:32,041
You wouldn't understand.

484
00:51:32,224 --> 00:51:34,320
You have no idea how painful it is to live with that kind of suffering.

485
00:51:34,926 --> 00:51:36,200
Why wouldn't I understand?

486
00:51:50,723 --> 00:51:51,724
You know what they say.

487
00:51:54,270 --> 00:51:55,560
Wounds need to be treated.

488
00:51:58,318 --> 00:51:59,454
Leave them untreated, and they become chronic.

489
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:02,293
You and I just have different ways of healing.

490
00:52:05,899 --> 00:52:06,900
How are they different?

491
00:52:07,515 --> 00:52:09,120
Maybe I can help you.

492
00:52:09,926 --> 00:52:10,927
Trust me.

493
00:52:13,083 --> 00:52:14,539
Go home with your father.

494
00:52:17,182 --> 00:52:18,920
Someone like you isn't cut out for this.

495
00:52:24,526 --> 00:52:26,040
Can you help me get close to Dongyang?

496
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:31,710
You can sleep on the couch tonight.

497
00:52:32,462 --> 00:52:34,046
I'll get you some clothes.

498
00:53:22,920 --> 00:53:24,238
Keep a close eye on Dongyang.

499
00:53:24,739 --> 00:53:26,920
I'll let you know when it's time... Dad.

500
00:55:08,840 --> 00:55:10,712
Do you want to heal people or kill  people?

501
00:55:11,280 --> 00:55:12,680
If you go any further down this path,

502
00:55:12,830 --> 00:55:14,681
there'll be no turning back, Hattha.

503
00:55:15,507 --> 00:55:17,808
Using the art of healing massage to kill people...

504
00:55:18,291 --> 00:55:20,100
the consequences will come back to haunt you.

505
00:55:20,574 --> 00:55:22,440
And you'll become the very kind of person you hate.

506
00:55:38,767 --> 00:55:40,000
What are you doing?

507
00:56:57,688 --> 00:56:58,689
He's dead.

508
00:56:59,523 --> 00:57:01,320
You can go home to your father now.

509
00:57:29,091 --> 00:57:30,226
Dongyang is dead.

510
00:57:30,439 --> 00:57:31,960
- It's all over.
- No, it's not.

511
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:34,360
You think I'm supposed to be grateful? Do you know how much I've endured,

512
00:57:34,482 --> 00:57:36,920
how hard I've trained just so I could kill him with my own hands?

513
00:57:37,280 --> 00:57:39,281
I told you, I don't want you to become like me.

514
00:57:43,968 --> 00:57:45,280
What's wrong with Master Tim's feet?

515
00:57:45,560 --> 00:57:47,520
Master Tim isn't someone you should mess with.

516
00:57:49,360 --> 00:57:50,440
Stay away from him.
